From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 01:34:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: resctrl: add membw.mb_max_lim and
 arch_has_mb_max_lim

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2150290

Add mb_max_lim and arch_has_mb_max_lim to struct resctrl_membw with
kernel-doc: MPAM MAX_LIM encoding (MPAMF_MBW_IDR), invalid elsewhere
unless arch sets arch_has_mb_max_lim.

Signed-off-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00747
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-6.17@5f94014ae4101945d456b91aa6cf7dcc1b5623e0
---
 include/linux/resctrl.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/resctrl.h b/include/linux/resctrl.h
index 9c51bcf9a17a..ca78f62afe62 100644
--- a/include/linux/resctrl.h
+++ b/include/linux/resctrl.h
@@ -248,11 +248,15 @@ enum membw_throttle_mode {
  * @min_bw:		Minimum memory bandwidth percentage user can request
  * @max_bw:		Maximum memory bandwidth value, used as the reset value
  * @bw_gran:		Granularity at which the memory bandwidth is allocated
+ * @mb_max_lim:		MPAM MAX_LIM encoding (MPAMF_MBW_IDR); invalid elsewhere
+ * @arch_has_mb_max_lim:True if mb_max_lim is supported
  */
 struct resctrl_membw {
 	u32				min_bw;
 	u32				max_bw;
 	u32				bw_gran;
+	u8				mb_max_lim;
+	bool				arch_has_mb_max_lim;
 };
 
 /**
